WEBVTT

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:20.914
I got nothing, sir.
No sign of Niobe or Ghost.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.624
Nothing but blue pills.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.459
Should we try to contact them?

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:26.586
Won't matter.
My gut says they're down.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.798
- We should start back.
- If that ship can fly, we need it.

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:31.466
I was afraid you'd say that.

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:34.302
Search every pipe, every hole,
every crack we know.

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:36.930
Sweep as wide as possible,
as fast as possible.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:40.809
- Lines are crawling with calamari.
- Then the sooner we find them the better.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.983
Thought you could use
something to eat.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.819
Thank you.

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:53.530
Any change?

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:56.407
No.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:02:01.329
- How is he?
- He's gonna be fine.

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:04.124
At least until he wakes up.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:08.461
- What do you mean?
- Captain has some questions for him.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.879
He'd better have some good answers.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:14.134
You see these cuts?
I think they're self-inflicted.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.346
- Why?
- VDTs maybe. I don't know.

00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:21.850
But like I said,
the answer better be good.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:28.189
Roland, I'd like to run
another search through the Matrix.

00:02:28.356 --> 00:02:30.567
- For what?
- For Neo.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.987
How could he be in the Matrix, sir?
He's not plugged in.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.488
Please, for me.

00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:48.710
This is what keeps bothering me.

00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:50.879
What?

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:54.716
His neural patterns don't read
like someone who's in a coma.

00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:57.844
The strange thing is,
I see these patterns all the time.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:01.347
- Where?
- On someone jacked in.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:16.321
The big <i>bupkes. Nada.</i>
He's not in there.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.740
- Sir, I got the projections.
- How long?

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:23.411
Based on point of entry and past speed,
the machines will be in Zion in 20 hours.

00:03:23.661 --> 00:03:26.247
Jesus H. Christ.

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:31.044
All right, let's move with a purpose.
AK, I want you on holographics.

00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:34.339
Mauser, I want forward and aft guns
manned at all times.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.633
Make sure we're running
on as few pads as possible.

00:03:36.841 --> 00:03:38.676
- Yes, sir.
- Hey.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.971
- Hey! You got a call.
- What?

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.558
Operator.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:48.269
It's Seraph.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:52.690
I bring word from the Oracle.
You must come at once.

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:10.166
- Where am I?
- This is the train station.

00:04:13.002 --> 00:04:16.255
- This isn't the Matrix?
- That's where the train goes.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:19.717
That's where we're going,
but you cannot go with us.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.888
- Why not?
- He won't let you.

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:28.601
- Who won't?
- The Trainman. I don't like him.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:32.105
But my papa says we have to do
what the Trainman says...

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:36.150
...or else he will leave us here
forever and ever.

00:04:50.748 --> 00:04:55.420
Morpheus, Trinity,
thank you for coming.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.339
One thing I've learned in all my years...

00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:01.634
...is that nothing ever works out
the way you want it to.

00:05:01.884 --> 00:05:04.846
- Who are you?
- I'm the Oracle.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:11.853
I wish there was an easy way to get
through this, but there ain't.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.939
I'm sorry this had to happen.

00:05:15.106 --> 00:05:18.651
I'm sorry I couldn't be sitting here
like you remember me...

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.779
- ...but it wasn't meant to be.
- What happened?

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:26.868
I made a choice, and that choice
cost me more than I wanted it to.

00:05:27.118 --> 00:05:28.453
What choice?

00:05:28.911 --> 00:05:31.706
To help you, to guide Neo.

00:05:31.914 --> 00:05:36.836
Now, since the real test for any choice is
having to make the same choice again...

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:40.798
...knowing full well
what it might cost...

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.551
...I guess I feel pretty good
about that choice...

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:48.014
...because here I am, at it again.

00:05:48.306 --> 00:05:52.060
- Do you know what happened to Neo?
- Yes.

00:05:52.435 --> 00:05:56.981
He is trapped in a place between
this world and the machine world.

00:05:57.315 --> 00:06:01.486
The link is controlled by a program
called the Trainman.

00:06:01.652 --> 00:06:06.157
He uses it to smuggle programs
in and out of the Matrix.

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:09.535
If he finds out where Neo is
before you get to him...

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:13.164
...then I'm afraid our choices
are going to become difficult.

00:06:13.331 --> 00:06:16.501
- Why?
- Because of who the Trainman works for.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.503
The Merovingian.

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:23.216
He has placed a bounty on your lives.
You must be careful at all times.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:27.929
Seraph knows how to find the Trainman.
He'll go with you.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:31.891
For years he has protected me.

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:34.560
I hope he can do the same for you.

00:06:35.686 --> 00:06:38.397
Please, follow me.

00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:45.029
Oracle...

00:06:45.196 --> 00:06:47.407
I know, Morpheus.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:51.285
I can see you're filled with doubt,
clouded by uncertainty.

00:06:51.494 --> 00:06:56.082
After everything that has happened,
how can you expect me to believe you?

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.000
I don't.

00:06:58.209 --> 00:07:00.878
I expect just what I've always expected:

00:07:01.045 --> 00:07:05.299
For you to make up your own
damn mind. Believe me or don't.

00:07:05.508 --> 00:07:10.888
All I can do is tell you that your friend
is in trouble, and he needs your help.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:14.475
He needs all our help.

00:07:15.059 --> 00:07:17.603
- Are you from the Matrix?
- Yes.

00:07:17.728 --> 00:07:19.105
No.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:23.151
- I mean, I was.
- Why did you leave?

00:07:24.068 --> 00:07:27.321
- I had to.
- I had to leave my home too.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:31.284
Sati! Come here, darling.
Leave the poor man in peace.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.952
Yes, Papa.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:41.460
I am sorry. She is still very curious.

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:45.423
- I know you.
- Yes, in the restaurant of the Frenchman.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:50.303
I am Rama-Kandra. This is my wife,
Kamala. My daughter, Sati.

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:52.472
We are most honored to meet you.

00:07:53.055 --> 00:07:55.266
- You are programs.
- Oh, yes.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:59.854
I am the power-plant systems manager
for recycling operations.

00:08:00.062 --> 00:08:04.108
My wife is an interactive software
programmer. She is highly creative.

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:06.777
What are you doing here?
You do not belong here.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:11.866
Kamala! Goodness, I apologize.
My wife can be very direct.

00:08:13.117 --> 00:08:14.660
It's okay.

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.496
I don't have an answer.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:20.166
- I don't even know where "here" is.
- This place is nowhere.

00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:23.127
It is between your world and our world.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.673
- Who's the Trainman?
- He works for the Frenchman.

00:08:28.132 --> 00:08:30.009
Why did I know
you were going to say that?

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:34.138
The Frenchman does not forget,
and he does not forgive.

00:08:34.597 --> 00:08:37.183
- You know him?
- I know only what I need to know.

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:41.354
I know if you want to take something
from our world into your world...

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.732
...that does not belong there,
you must go to the Frenchman.

00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:46.526
Is that what you're doing here?

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:50.696
- Rama, please.
- I do not want to be cruel, Kamala.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:53.407
He may never see another face
for the rest of his life.

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:55.660
I'm sorry.

00:08:55.826 --> 00:08:59.080
- You don't have to answer that question.
- No, I don't mind.

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:02.041
The answer is simple.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.007
I love my daughter very much.

00:09:10.174 --> 00:09:13.678
I find her to be the most beautiful thing
I have ever seen.

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:16.555
But where we are from,
that is not enough.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:19.392
Every program that is created
must have a purpose.

00:09:19.642 --> 00:09:22.937
If it does not, it is deleted.

00:09:23.145 --> 00:09:26.774
I went to the Frenchman
to save my daughter.

00:09:28.401 --> 00:09:31.737
- You do not understand.
- I just have never...

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:34.240
Heard a program speak of love.

00:09:35.032 --> 00:09:38.494
- It is a human emotion.
- No, it is a word.

00:09:39.537 --> 00:09:43.916
What matters is the connection
the word implies.

00:09:46.377 --> 00:09:49.338
I see that you are in love.

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:53.926
Can you tell me what you would give
to hold on to that connection?

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:55.428
Anything.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.597
Then perhaps the reason you are here...

00:09:57.763 --> 00:10:01.058
...is not so different
than the reason I am here.

00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:10.651
That's him.

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:14.655
- Get away! Get away from me!
- We don't want trouble.

00:10:14.864 --> 00:10:17.783
- Get the hell away from me!
- We need your help.

00:10:17.908 --> 00:10:21.495
I can't help you!
No one can help you!

00:11:12.505 --> 00:11:14.006
Oh, no!

00:11:26.352 --> 00:11:27.937
Damn it!

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:35.027
- When is the train due?
- It is already late.

00:11:35.194 --> 00:11:37.363
It's not like the Trainman to be late.

00:11:37.988 --> 00:11:40.032
You think it has something
to do with me?

00:11:40.157 --> 00:11:41.534
I cannot say.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.537
Who knows such things?
Only the Oracle.

00:11:44.704 --> 00:11:47.540
- You know the Oracle?
- Everyone knows the Oracle.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.501
I consulted with her
before I met with the Frenchman.

00:11:50.668 --> 00:11:53.212
She promised she'd look after Sati
after we said goodbye.

00:11:53.337 --> 00:11:55.381
Goodbye?

00:11:55.548 --> 00:11:58.217
- You're not staying with her?
- It is not possible.

00:11:58.384 --> 00:12:02.388
Our arrangement with the Frenchman
was for our daughter only.

00:12:02.555 --> 00:12:06.058
- My wife and I must return to our world.
- Why?

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:09.228
- That is our karma.
- You believe in karma?

00:12:09.395 --> 00:12:12.606
Karma is a word, like love.

00:12:12.815 --> 00:12:14.567
A way of saying:

00:12:14.817 --> 00:12:17.027
"What I am here to do."

00:12:17.194 --> 00:12:20.781
I do not resent my karma.
I'm grateful for it.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:24.410
Grateful for my wonderful wife,
for my beautiful daughter.

00:12:24.577 --> 00:12:28.747
They are gifts, and so I do
what I must do to honor them.

00:12:30.332 --> 00:12:33.752
- Papa, the train!
- Yes. Find your bag. Quickly.

00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:38.757
Can I carry that for you?

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:41.927
All right.

00:12:47.349 --> 00:12:48.642
Hurry it up, I'm late!

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:55.065
Who are you?

00:12:55.274 --> 00:12:56.984
- He is a friend.
- Rama!

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.613
I know you.

00:13:00.738 --> 00:13:04.450
- So that's what they wanted.
- I need to get back.

00:13:05.618 --> 00:13:07.995
- I'll pay you whatever you want.
- Oh.

00:13:08.204 --> 00:13:10.623
One way or another,
I'm getting on this train.

00:13:10.873 --> 00:13:12.500
Oh, no, no, no.

00:13:12.708 --> 00:13:15.628
You'll stay right here until
the Merovingian says different.

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:17.296
If I know him...

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:20.966
...you're gonna be here
for a long, long time.

00:13:21.383 --> 00:13:25.179
- I don't want to hurt you.
- You don't get it.

00:13:25.387 --> 00:13:27.973
I built this place.

00:13:28.098 --> 00:13:32.478
Down here, I make the rules.
Down here, I make the threats.

00:13:39.652 --> 00:13:43.364
Get on the train
or you'll stay here with him.

00:13:59.213 --> 00:14:02.132
We should return to the Oracle.
She will know what to do.

00:14:02.341 --> 00:14:05.094
No. We know what has to be done.

00:14:20.901 --> 00:14:22.152
Shit.

00:14:50.472 --> 00:14:52.933
You gotta be kidding.

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.144
Holy shit, it's wingless.

00:14:55.936 --> 00:14:57.479
I get it.

00:14:57.605 --> 00:15:00.482
You must be ready to die.

00:15:00.774 --> 00:15:02.318
I need to speak with him.

00:15:02.484 --> 00:15:07.114
Only way you're getting through
this door is over my big, dead ass.

00:15:07.948 --> 00:15:09.283
So be it.

00:15:32.514 --> 00:15:34.892
There are no weapons allowed
in the club.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:38.520
At the bottom of this elevator,
there is a coat-check girl...

00:15:38.687 --> 00:15:41.857
...and if we are lucky,
one man for checking weapons.

00:15:42.358 --> 00:15:44.193
And if we're unlucky?

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.236
There will be many men.

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:50.741
Can I take your...? Oh, my God.

00:18:12.508 --> 00:18:15.010
What in the hell?

00:18:17.763 --> 00:18:19.556
I don't believe this.

00:18:25.521 --> 00:18:28.398
Hey! Hey!

00:18:31.193 --> 00:18:34.154
The prodigal child returns.

00:18:36.782 --> 00:18:40.410
Are you here for the bounty, Seraph?

00:18:42.496 --> 00:18:45.374
Tell me, how many bullets
are there in those guns?

00:18:45.541 --> 00:18:48.710
I don't know, but I don't think
you have enough.

00:18:48.877 --> 00:18:51.713
- We only want to talk.
- Oh, yes.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:57.219
I'm sure you do. You have fought
through Hel to do so. Yes?

00:18:57.636 --> 00:18:59.596
I'll tell you what I will do.

00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:03.725
Put down the guns, and I will promise
you a safe passage out of here.

00:19:04.143 --> 00:19:06.562
- All three of us?
- Oh, yes, yes.

00:19:07.646 --> 00:19:09.439
Of course.

00:19:35.507 --> 00:19:41.263
Who could have guessed we'd see each
other so soon after our last meeting?

00:19:41.597 --> 00:19:44.474
The Fates are too kind, eh?

00:19:44.683 --> 00:19:48.145
And since you, my little Judas,
have brought them here...

00:19:48.353 --> 00:19:53.150
...I can only surmise the fortuneteller
has found herself another shell?

00:19:53.358 --> 00:19:56.612
Disappointing, but not unexpected.

00:19:56.778 --> 00:20:00.282
I do hope, however, she has the good
manners to learn her lesson...

00:20:00.449 --> 00:20:03.744
...and to remember that there is
no action without consequence.

00:20:03.952 --> 00:20:08.081
And if you take something from me,
you will pay the price.

00:20:09.207 --> 00:20:12.002
You know why we are here?

00:20:12.628 --> 00:20:15.797
Come now, what kind of question
is this? Of course I know.

00:20:15.964 --> 00:20:18.008
It is my business to know.

00:20:18.216 --> 00:20:21.470
Some might think this is a strange
coincidence, but I do not.

00:20:21.887 --> 00:20:28.143
I am curious, though,
as to how it actually happened.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:30.479
- Do you know?
- No.

00:20:30.604 --> 00:20:32.356
No?

00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:34.691
I did not think so.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.819
But it is always best to ask, huh?

00:20:37.945 --> 00:20:40.030
We want to make a deal.

00:20:41.573 --> 00:20:45.994
Always straight to business,
huh, Morpheus?

00:20:46.161 --> 00:20:50.499
Okay. I have something you want.

00:20:50.666 --> 00:20:52.668
To make a deal...

00:20:52.834 --> 00:20:58.340
...you must have something
I want, yes?

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:02.844
And it so happens
there is something I want.

00:21:03.011 --> 00:21:07.349
Something I have wanted
ever since I first came here.

00:21:07.599 --> 00:21:10.352
It is said they cannot be taken...

00:21:10.769 --> 00:21:13.063
...they can only be given.

00:21:13.272 --> 00:21:14.564
What?

00:21:17.109 --> 00:21:19.569
The eyes of the Oracle.

00:21:23.365 --> 00:21:26.910
I told you before, there is no escaping
the nature of the universe.

00:21:27.119 --> 00:21:29.871
It is that nature
that has again brought you to me.

00:21:30.038 --> 00:21:33.709
Where some see coincidence,
I see consequence.

00:21:33.834 --> 00:21:36.169
Where others see chance...

00:21:36.336 --> 00:21:39.881
...I see cost.

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:45.345
Bring me the eyes of the Oracle...

00:21:45.846 --> 00:21:48.765
...and I will give you back your savior.

00:21:49.391 --> 00:21:53.729
It seems a perfectly fair
and reasonable deal to me.

00:21:54.479 --> 00:21:55.772
Yes? No?

00:21:58.233 --> 00:21:59.943
I don't have time for this shit.

00:22:31.767 --> 00:22:34.436
You wanna make a deal?
How about this?

00:22:34.686 --> 00:22:38.732
You give me Neo, or we all die,
right here, right now.

00:22:39.691 --> 00:22:42.611
Interesting deal.

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:49.618
You are really ready to die
for this man?

00:22:50.744 --> 00:22:53.330
- Believe it.
- She'll do it.

00:22:53.914 --> 00:22:56.750
If she has to,
she'll kill every one of us.

00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:58.377
She's in love.

00:22:59.294 --> 00:23:04.633
It is remarkable how similar the pattern
of love is to the pattern of insanity.

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:06.385
Time's up.

00:23:06.593 --> 00:23:08.095
What's it gonna be, Merv?

00:23:12.766 --> 00:23:16.603
Okay. You got yourself in here...

00:23:16.812 --> 00:23:19.356
...you can get yourself out.

00:24:07.028 --> 00:24:08.363
Are you ready for us?

00:24:08.530 --> 00:24:11.533
Almost, sir. They got
some pretty ancient hacks here.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:13.869
- But you found Neo?
- Can't you see him?

00:24:13.994 --> 00:24:16.913
No, sir. We were reading something,
but I couldn't tell what.

00:24:21.543 --> 00:24:23.044
I can't leave yet.

00:24:26.047 --> 00:24:28.383
I have to see her.

00:24:29.050 --> 00:24:31.261
Now?

00:24:32.387 --> 00:24:33.763
It's my last chance.

00:24:36.391 --> 00:24:38.727
That's it. That's the secret.

00:24:38.894 --> 00:24:41.062
- You've got to use your hands.
- Why?

00:24:41.563 --> 00:24:44.232
Cookies need love like everything does.

00:24:46.026 --> 00:24:47.444
Neo!

00:24:47.861 --> 00:24:52.741
I was hoping to have these done
before you got here. Oh, well.

00:24:53.825 --> 00:24:56.870
Sati, honey, I think it's time
for a tasting.

00:24:57.162 --> 00:25:00.040
Take the bowl to Seraph
and find out if they're ready.

00:25:00.207 --> 00:25:02.292
Okay.

00:25:02.918 --> 00:25:05.420
- I'm glad you got out.
- Me too.

00:25:09.341 --> 00:25:12.677
So do you recognize me?

00:25:12.886 --> 00:25:16.097
- A part of you.
- Yeah, that's how it works.

00:25:16.264 --> 00:25:19.100
Some bits you lose,
some bits you keep.

00:25:19.267 --> 00:25:23.104
I don't yet recognize my face
in the mirror...

00:25:24.689 --> 00:25:26.608
...but I still love candy.

00:25:29.110 --> 00:25:30.403
No, thank you.

00:25:30.612 --> 00:25:33.782
Remember what you were like
when you first walked through my door?

00:25:33.949 --> 00:25:38.995
Jittery as a June bug.
And now, just look at you.

00:25:39.204 --> 00:25:42.457
You sure did surprise me, Neo,
and you still do.

00:25:42.874 --> 00:25:45.919
You gave me a few surprises too.

00:25:46.086 --> 00:25:48.338
I hope I helped.

00:25:48.546 --> 00:25:51.967
You helped me to get here,
but my question is, why?

00:25:52.217 --> 00:25:53.927
Where is this going?

00:25:54.094 --> 00:25:56.638
- Where does it end?
- I don't know.

00:25:56.930 --> 00:26:00.308
- You don't know or you won't tell me?
- I told you before...

00:26:00.809 --> 00:26:05.814
...no one can see beyond a choice they
don't understand, and I mean no one.

00:26:06.439 --> 00:26:10.318
- What choice?
- It doesn't matter. It's my choice.

00:26:10.443 --> 00:26:12.988
I have mine to make,
same as you have yours.

00:26:13.280 --> 00:26:16.157
Does that include what things
to tell me and what not to?

00:26:16.324 --> 00:26:17.534
Of course not.

00:26:17.742 --> 00:26:19.953
Then why didn't you tell me
about the Architect?

00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:24.332
About Zion and the ones before me?
Why didn't you tell me the truth?

00:26:25.292 --> 00:26:29.170
- Because it wasn't time for you to know.
- Who decided it wasn't time?

00:26:29.629 --> 00:26:32.215
You know who.

00:26:38.972 --> 00:26:41.182
I did.

00:26:41.683 --> 00:26:45.020
Then I think it's time for me to know
a few more things.

00:26:45.145 --> 00:26:46.896
So do I.

00:26:47.272 --> 00:26:50.984
Tell me how I separated my mind
from my body without jacking in.

00:26:51.192 --> 00:26:53.903
Tell me how I stopped four sentinels
by thinking it.

00:26:54.529 --> 00:26:58.199
Tell me just what the hell
is happening to me.

00:27:00.327 --> 00:27:03.872
The power of the One
extends beyond this world.

00:27:04.039 --> 00:27:07.542
It reaches from here all the way back
to where it came from.

00:27:07.709 --> 00:27:09.961
- Where?
- The source.

00:27:10.170 --> 00:27:14.841
That's what you felt when you touched
those sentinels, but you weren't ready.

00:27:15.342 --> 00:27:20.930
You should be dead, but apparently
you weren't ready for that either.

00:27:22.891 --> 00:27:25.727
The Architect told me that
if I didn't return to the source...

00:27:25.894 --> 00:27:27.729
...Zion would be destroyed tonight.

00:27:27.854 --> 00:27:32.233
Please. You and I may not be able
to see beyond our own choices...

00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:35.111
...but that man can't see
past any choice.

00:27:35.653 --> 00:27:39.407
- Why not?
- He doesn't understand them. He can't.

00:27:39.574 --> 00:27:42.243
To him, they are variables
in an equation.

00:27:42.410 --> 00:27:46.414
One at a time, each variable
must be solved, then countered.

00:27:46.581 --> 00:27:50.293
That's his purpose.
To balance the equation.

00:27:50.752 --> 00:27:52.837
What's your purpose?

00:27:53.046 --> 00:27:55.090
To unbalance it.

00:27:55.215 --> 00:27:57.300
Why? What do you want?

00:27:57.884 --> 00:28:01.429
I want the same thing you want, Neo.

00:28:01.554 --> 00:28:04.474
And I'm willing to go
as far as you are to get it.

00:28:05.016 --> 00:28:07.477
The end of the war.

00:28:08.103 --> 00:28:09.562
Is it going to end?

00:28:10.355 --> 00:28:12.440
One way or another.

00:28:13.024 --> 00:28:16.361
Can Zion be saved?

00:28:16.778 --> 00:28:21.574
I'm sorry, I don't have the answer
to that question, but...

00:28:22.450 --> 00:28:27.288
If there is an answer, there's only
one place you're going to find it.

00:28:27.539 --> 00:28:30.166
- Where?
- You know where.

00:28:32.127 --> 00:28:35.255
And if you can't find the answer...

00:28:35.463 --> 00:28:38.967
...then I'm afraid there may be
no tomorrow for any of us.

00:28:40.593 --> 00:28:43.304
What does that mean?

00:28:47.308 --> 00:28:50.937
Everything that has a beginning...

00:28:51.104 --> 00:28:53.523
...has an end.

00:28:53.732 --> 00:28:56.651
I see the end coming.

00:28:56.818 --> 00:28:59.696
I see the darkness spreading.

00:28:59.904 --> 00:29:01.322
I see death.

00:29:02.073 --> 00:29:05.618
And you are all that stands in his way.

00:29:05.785 --> 00:29:07.120
Smith.

00:29:08.079 --> 00:29:12.375
Very soon, he is going to have the power
to destroy this world.

00:29:12.584 --> 00:29:15.295
But I believe he won't stop there.
He can't.

00:29:15.503 --> 00:29:18.548
He won't stop until
there's nothing left at all.

00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:20.216
What is he?

00:29:20.425 --> 00:29:22.343
He is you.

00:29:22.510 --> 00:29:24.971
Your opposite, your negative.

00:29:25.138 --> 00:29:28.683
The result of the equation
trying to balance itself out.

00:29:29.017 --> 00:29:32.896
- And if I can't stop him?
- One way or another, Neo...

00:29:33.688 --> 00:29:36.983
...this war is going to end.

00:29:37.150 --> 00:29:42.030
Tonight, the future of both worlds
will be in your hands...

00:29:42.197 --> 00:29:43.990
...or in his.

00:30:00.507 --> 00:30:03.092
How are you feeling?
Are you all right?

00:30:10.225 --> 00:30:12.560
I need time.

00:30:17.232 --> 00:30:20.777
- That figures.
- Captain Roland.

00:30:20.985 --> 00:30:23.279
- What's up, Maggie?
- Bane is. He's conscious.

00:30:23.488 --> 00:30:25.615
Good. Maybe he's got some answers.

00:30:30.703 --> 00:30:32.580
Mm!

00:30:32.747 --> 00:30:35.625
I love that smell.

00:30:36.709 --> 00:30:39.754
I sure am going to miss it.

00:30:40.421 --> 00:30:43.424
- Oracle.
- I know.

00:30:43.675 --> 00:30:44.926
I know.

00:30:45.176 --> 00:30:47.804
Sati, honey.

00:30:48.930 --> 00:30:51.224
Take a few cookies and go with Seraph.

00:30:51.432 --> 00:30:54.227
Can I come back?
I would like to come back.

00:30:54.394 --> 00:30:57.772
- I would like that too.
- Then I'll see you tomorrow.

00:31:00.191 --> 00:31:02.944
I hope so, hon, I hope so.

00:31:25.466 --> 00:31:26.968
I'm scared, Seraph.

00:31:28.595 --> 00:31:30.471
Come.

00:32:13.598 --> 00:32:16.351
He's following us.

00:32:20.521 --> 00:32:24.359
Well, well, it's been a long time.

00:32:25.860 --> 00:32:28.863
I remember chasing you
was like chasing a ghost.

00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:31.032
I have beaten you before.

00:32:31.532 --> 00:32:36.120
Yes, true, but as you can see,
things are a little different now.

00:32:37.872 --> 00:32:40.875
And you must be the last exile.

00:32:41.542 --> 00:32:45.046
- The Oracle told me about you.
- Really?

00:32:45.296 --> 00:32:47.131
What did she say about me?

00:32:47.548 --> 00:32:49.258
That you were a bad man.

00:32:49.550 --> 00:32:54.263
Oh, I'm not so bad,
once you get to know me.

00:33:22.917 --> 00:33:27.463
The great and powerful Oracle,
we meet at last.

00:33:30.383 --> 00:33:34.762
I suppose you've been
expecting me, right?

00:33:34.929 --> 00:33:37.306
The all-knowing Oracle
is never surprised.

00:33:37.515 --> 00:33:40.643
How can she be? She knows everything.

00:33:41.394 --> 00:33:45.565
But if that's true, then why is she here
if she knew I was coming?

00:33:45.732 --> 00:33:47.734
Why wouldn't she leave?

00:33:53.281 --> 00:33:55.783
Maybe you knew I would do that,
maybe you didn't.

00:33:55.950 --> 00:33:59.495
If you did, that means you baked those
cookies and set that plate there...

00:33:59.704 --> 00:34:01.414
...deliberately, purposefully...

00:34:01.581 --> 00:34:05.585
...which means that you're sitting there
also deliberately, purposefully.

00:34:06.627 --> 00:34:08.463
What did you do with Sati?

00:34:09.213 --> 00:34:13.801
"Cookies need love
like everything does."

00:34:15.803 --> 00:34:17.263
You are a bastard.

00:34:18.097 --> 00:34:20.475
You would know, Mom.

00:34:24.604 --> 00:34:26.647
Do what you're here to do.

00:34:27.148 --> 00:34:29.150
Yes, ma'am.

00:35:13.820 --> 00:35:18.324
I really wish I could help, but I just...
I don't remember any of it.

00:35:20.034 --> 00:35:23.913
What about the cuts on your arms?
Those cuts are more than one day old.

00:35:24.539 --> 00:35:27.125
Yeah, definitely.

00:35:27.333 --> 00:35:29.585
You're right about that, sir.

00:35:30.127 --> 00:35:33.422
They look like they
might be self-inflicted.

00:35:33.631 --> 00:35:37.844
But why would I do something
like that to myself?

00:35:38.052 --> 00:35:42.890
Unless, of course, I wasn't myself.

00:35:43.057 --> 00:35:47.728
But if I'm not me, then who am I?

00:35:52.483 --> 00:35:56.571
- Has this man been tested for VDTs?
- Yes, sir. It was negative.

00:35:57.321 --> 00:36:00.449
But he is showing a lot
of unusual neural activity.

00:36:00.658 --> 00:36:03.953
Some cross-synaptic firing,
as well as signs of recent trauma...

00:36:04.162 --> 00:36:07.957
...with fresh fibrotic scarring
throughout the cortex.

00:36:08.332 --> 00:36:12.962
I want the truth. I don't care
what it takes. Make him remember.

00:36:34.442 --> 00:36:35.735
Sir, we found her.

00:36:35.943 --> 00:36:37.278
- The <i>Logos</i>?
- Yes, sir.

00:36:37.403 --> 00:36:39.488
About time we had
some goddamn good news.

00:37:09.644 --> 00:37:12.647
Are the thermals picking up
any signs of life?

00:37:13.648 --> 00:37:15.274
No, sir. Nothing yet.

00:37:15.483 --> 00:37:19.111
- What about the ship?
- Holographic says the hull's intact.

00:37:19.278 --> 00:37:22.323
- Drop down and keep a man in the turret.
- Yes, sir.

00:37:32.667 --> 00:37:36.545
Get a full diagnostic on that ship
as fast as humanly possible.

00:37:54.313 --> 00:37:55.690
Careful, sir.

00:37:56.107 --> 00:38:00.361
The squids are sneaky bastards.
It could be a trap.

00:38:25.886 --> 00:38:27.888
What was that?

00:38:29.890 --> 00:38:33.060
You can put that shit away,
boys. All she needs is a jump.

00:38:34.729 --> 00:38:37.732
- Niobe.
- Morpheus.

00:38:41.694 --> 00:38:44.071
- Are you all right?
- Yes, I'm fine.

00:38:44.238 --> 00:38:47.074
We didn't know what happened after...

00:38:48.909 --> 00:38:52.038
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

00:38:52.204 --> 00:38:54.248
I'm happy to see you too.

00:38:55.082 --> 00:38:56.959
- Did you get Neo out?
- Yes.

00:38:57.168 --> 00:38:59.295
- How did you know about that?
- The Oracle.

00:38:59.503 --> 00:39:02.089
- You saw her?
- Just before the sentinels found us.

00:39:02.590 --> 00:39:06.761
- What did she tell you?
- The same thing she always does.

00:39:07.928 --> 00:39:10.765
Exactly what I needed to hear.

00:39:12.391 --> 00:39:15.269
In 12 hours, the machines
will breach the dock walls.

00:39:15.603 --> 00:39:19.940
Every simulation we've run, we've seen
that once the machines are inside...

00:39:20.107 --> 00:39:22.777
...the odds of our survival
decrease dramatically.

00:39:22.943 --> 00:39:24.904
Thus, our primary objective must be...

00:39:25.112 --> 00:39:28.574
...to destroy or disable the diggers
inside the dock.

00:39:28.741 --> 00:39:32.953
If we can do that, perhaps we can
prevent them from reaching the city.

00:39:33.120 --> 00:39:36.290
If not, the only place we will be able
to mount a defense...

00:39:36.457 --> 00:39:38.584
...will be at the entrance of the temple.

00:39:38.793 --> 00:39:41.504
It is small and will force
them into a bottleneck...

00:39:41.712 --> 00:39:44.799
...allowing us to concentrate
the remainder of our defense.

00:39:45.132 --> 00:39:48.135
We understand that you've requested
additional volunteers.

00:39:48.302 --> 00:39:50.805
- That is correct.
- Precisely what size force...

00:39:50.971 --> 00:39:54.225
...are you planning to commit
to the primary dock objective?

00:39:54.433 --> 00:39:57.978
Right now, the entire APU Corps
and half the infantry.

00:39:58.104 --> 00:40:01.148
- Half the infantry?
- If it were up to me, councillor...

00:40:01.273 --> 00:40:04.610
...I'd take every man, woman and child,
put a gun in their hand...

00:40:04.777 --> 00:40:06.654
...and march them into that dock.

00:40:06.821 --> 00:40:09.532
Perhaps it is best
that it is not up to you.

00:40:09.740 --> 00:40:11.700
Time will tell, councillor.

00:40:11.992 --> 00:40:14.662
Commander, just one more question.

00:40:14.829 --> 00:40:17.123
Has there been word
from the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i>?

00:40:17.289 --> 00:40:20.709
None, and at this point there's no reason
to expect there will be.

00:40:20.918 --> 00:40:22.878
Perhaps.

00:40:23.087 --> 00:40:24.463
But we can hope.

00:40:24.839 --> 00:40:28.050
I'm afraid hope is an indulgence
I don't have time for.

00:40:39.395 --> 00:40:42.273
What the shit is going on over here?

00:40:42.439 --> 00:40:45.943
An accident, sir. I didn't see...

00:40:46.110 --> 00:40:48.279
- I'm sorry.
- Who the hell are you?

00:40:48.446 --> 00:40:50.739
A unit volunteer, sir.

00:40:51.365 --> 00:40:55.119
What's a pod-born pencil-neck like you
doing volunteering for my Corps?

00:40:55.786 --> 00:40:59.290
I want to do my part, sir.
We gotta hold the dock.

00:41:00.624 --> 00:41:02.710
- How old are you, kid?
- Eighteen.

00:41:02.918 --> 00:41:06.005
Should have said 16,
I might have believed that.

00:41:06.297 --> 00:41:07.590
Okay, I'm 16.

00:41:07.798 --> 00:41:11.343
Minimum age for the Corps is 18.
Sixteen's too young.

00:41:11.552 --> 00:41:16.348
The machines don't care how old I am.
They'll kill me just the same.

00:41:16.974 --> 00:41:18.851
Ain't that the goddamn truth.

00:41:19.393 --> 00:41:22.646
Give me a chance, sir.
I won't let you down.

00:41:23.397 --> 00:41:24.732
You do...

00:41:24.982 --> 00:41:28.527
...and you'll find me and the machines
have got something in common.

00:41:41.499 --> 00:41:44.168
Okay, charge the igniter.

00:41:50.299 --> 00:41:52.176
She lives again.

00:41:52.509 --> 00:41:55.679
Want us to patch an uplink to reload
the operations software, Sparky?

00:41:55.846 --> 00:41:59.183
That'd be swell. Could you clean
the windshield while you're at it?

00:42:03.979 --> 00:42:06.565
Uplinks in place.
I'm bringing her back online.

00:42:06.774 --> 00:42:09.527
Looking good, except, uh...

00:42:11.320 --> 00:42:13.364
Something's wrong
with the Matrix feed.

00:42:13.531 --> 00:42:16.742
No, there's not. You're looking
at what we're looking at.

00:42:16.951 --> 00:42:20.412
<i>- What's going on in there?</i>
- Whatever it is, it can't be good.

00:42:21.455 --> 00:42:23.415
The machines have taken Junction 21.

00:42:24.375 --> 00:42:27.461
The way I see it, if we drop down
from broadcast here...

00:42:27.670 --> 00:42:30.256
...intersect 153, we might surprise them.

00:42:30.839 --> 00:42:35.052
We'll go first, hammer as deep
as we can, then blow our EMP.

00:42:35.219 --> 00:42:39.223
Hopefully we can punch a hole
big enough for you to get through.

00:42:40.724 --> 00:42:45.562
It ain't pretty, but the way I see it,
it's the only way back.

00:42:45.729 --> 00:42:47.189
No, it's not.

00:42:47.398 --> 00:42:50.442
There's another way. A support line.

00:42:50.651 --> 00:42:54.405
It drops down right here,
1000 meters short of 21.

00:42:54.697 --> 00:42:58.576
If we're lucky, we may be able to
slip down without them ever knowing.

00:42:58.742 --> 00:43:01.203
That's a mechanical line.
It's impossible.

00:43:01.370 --> 00:43:03.414
- No one can pilot mechanical.
- I can.

00:43:03.539 --> 00:43:05.582
- Bullshit.
- I've done it.

00:43:05.749 --> 00:43:08.961
- That was a long time ago, Niobe.
- I said I can do it.

00:43:09.169 --> 00:43:13.757
So what? You'll be the only one that can.
There's no way we can follow you.

00:43:16.260 --> 00:43:17.845
Hi.

00:43:19.513 --> 00:43:24.059
I know time is always against us.
I'm sorry that I took so long.

00:43:24.268 --> 00:43:28.063
- But I wanted to be sure.
- Sure of what?

00:43:28.230 --> 00:43:30.316
- I know what I have to do.
- What?

00:43:30.524 --> 00:43:33.777
There's no easy way to say this,
so I'll just say it.

00:43:33.944 --> 00:43:36.614
- I have to take one of the ships.
- What?

00:43:36.739 --> 00:43:38.490
To go where?

00:43:39.450 --> 00:43:40.784
To the machine city.

00:43:45.539 --> 00:43:47.625
I know it's difficult to understand.

00:43:47.750 --> 00:43:50.294
No, it's not. You're out
of your goddamn mind.

00:43:50.627 --> 00:43:51.962
I still have to go.

00:43:52.129 --> 00:43:55.299
In 100 years, no ship has been
within 100 kilometers of it.

00:43:55.549 --> 00:43:58.177
- You'll never make it.
- I have to try.

00:43:58.385 --> 00:44:01.347
- Is this what the Oracle has told you?
- No.

00:44:02.056 --> 00:44:04.850
This is asinine. If you want
to kill yourself, do it...

00:44:05.059 --> 00:44:07.144
...but do it without
wasting our ships.

00:44:07.269 --> 00:44:10.272
- You have to believe me. I have to go.
- Bullshit!

00:44:10.439 --> 00:44:13.609
I am the captain of this ship.
I say where it has to go!

00:44:13.817 --> 00:44:17.654
And this ship will go to hell
long before I let you take it anywhere.

00:44:21.325 --> 00:44:25.329
- He can take mine.
- You can't do that.

00:44:26.330 --> 00:44:29.291
Don't try to tell me
what I can or cannot do...

00:44:29.458 --> 00:44:31.710
...with my ship
after that little speech.

00:44:31.919 --> 00:44:36.340
- But for chrissake, Niobe...
- I'll pilot this ship, he can take mine.

00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:40.469
If we leave inside the hour,
we'll reach Zion as the machines do.

00:44:40.678 --> 00:44:43.180
That's as good a plan as any.

00:44:43.347 --> 00:44:47.101
It's a waste. A goddamn waste.

00:44:52.689 --> 00:44:55.859
Two ships, two directions.

00:44:56.026 --> 00:44:59.196
Sounds like providence,
doesn't it, Morpheus?

00:44:59.863 --> 00:45:03.033
- You've never believed in the One.
- I still don't.

00:45:03.200 --> 00:45:04.868
Then why are you doing this?

00:45:06.495 --> 00:45:08.080
I believe in him.

00:45:09.873 --> 00:45:11.917
Thank you.

00:45:16.839 --> 00:45:19.883
- What's that for?
- To help you relax.

00:45:20.008 --> 00:45:22.886
To make it easier for you to remember.

00:45:23.554 --> 00:45:25.723
What if I don't want to remember?

00:45:26.723 --> 00:45:28.767
Why would you want that?

00:45:28.976 --> 00:45:32.062
What if I blew that EMP?

00:45:33.147 --> 00:45:35.065
What if I did destroy those ships....

00:45:35.232 --> 00:45:40.028
...and I am responsible
for the deaths of all those men?

00:45:42.072 --> 00:45:45.075
If I did that...

00:45:45.242 --> 00:45:48.954
...it wouldn't be very safe
for me here, would it?

00:45:58.839 --> 00:46:03.093
Of course, it might not be
very safe for you either.

00:46:10.934 --> 00:46:13.103
I'm ready.

00:46:14.188 --> 00:46:16.148
Trinity...

00:46:17.107 --> 00:46:19.776
...there's something I have to say.

00:46:22.863 --> 00:46:25.657
Something you need to understand.

00:46:26.867 --> 00:46:29.745
I know I'm supposed to go.

00:46:29.912 --> 00:46:32.164
But beyond that...

00:46:33.207 --> 00:46:35.626
...I don't know. I...

00:46:35.792 --> 00:46:39.671
I know. You don't think
you're coming back.

00:46:41.465 --> 00:46:46.303
I knew it the moment you said you had
to leave. I could see it in your face.

00:46:46.470 --> 00:46:49.139
Just like you knew the moment
you looked at me...

00:46:49.306 --> 00:46:51.683
...that I was coming with you.

00:46:53.810 --> 00:46:55.521
I'm scared, Trin.

00:46:55.896 --> 00:46:57.814
So am I.

00:46:58.649 --> 00:47:02.319
It took me 10 minutes
to buckle up one boot.

00:47:03.320 --> 00:47:05.364
But I'll tell you something.

00:47:05.572 --> 00:47:08.450
Six hours ago, I told the Merovingian...

00:47:08.659 --> 00:47:11.620
...I was ready to give anything
and everything for you.

00:47:14.164 --> 00:47:16.750
Do you know what's changed
in the last six hours?

00:47:16.959 --> 00:47:18.460
No.

00:47:19.002 --> 00:47:20.337
Nothing.

00:47:33.767 --> 00:47:36.019
<i>- Finished loading ammunition?</i>
- Just about.

00:47:36.270 --> 00:47:38.522
Let's move it. We are out of time.

00:47:38.772 --> 00:47:41.024
You're not leaving them anything?

00:47:41.149 --> 00:47:43.360
He said he didn't need it.

00:47:47.281 --> 00:47:50.659
I ain't saying goodbye.
I'm saying good luck.

00:47:51.118 --> 00:47:52.911
Thank you.

00:47:57.791 --> 00:48:00.669
I can only hope you know
what you're doing.

00:48:00.877 --> 00:48:02.254
Me too.

00:48:06.508 --> 00:48:08.010
It was an honor, sir.

00:48:12.306 --> 00:48:14.349
No, the honor is still mine.

00:48:28.238 --> 00:48:31.283
<i>- We're ready, sir.</i>
- About damn time.

00:48:32.534 --> 00:48:36.079
We're already late, captain,
so let's hit it and hit it hard.

00:48:39.833 --> 00:48:41.710
Bye, baby.

00:48:41.919 --> 00:48:43.754
Take good care of them.

00:49:05.567 --> 00:49:07.319
Ready?

00:49:15.118 --> 00:49:17.120
Engine's still firing.

00:49:17.371 --> 00:49:19.957
Must be a fuse. I'll check it out.

00:49:49.653 --> 00:49:52.739
Neo, it's Bane. He's psychotic!

00:49:53.573 --> 00:49:56.118
You're gonna pay for that.

00:49:57.327 --> 00:50:00.247
- Twenty-seven kilometers to go.
<i>- We got an emergency.</i>

00:50:00.414 --> 00:50:02.916
- What is it, AK?
<i>- It's Maggie, sir.</i>

00:50:03.083 --> 00:50:05.252
<i>She's dead, murdered.
I think it was Bane.</i>

00:50:05.419 --> 00:50:07.921
Goddamn it.

00:50:09.881 --> 00:50:13.260
I knew it. I knew he was
out of his goddamn mind.

00:50:13.427 --> 00:50:15.262
He fired that EMP.

00:50:15.429 --> 00:50:19.099
Goddamn it, I should have
beaten it out of him.

00:50:19.266 --> 00:50:22.144
We searched the whole ship, captain.
He ain't here.

00:50:23.854 --> 00:50:26.148
- I know where he is.
- The <i>Logos.</i>

00:50:27.858 --> 00:50:29.609
- We gotta go back.
- Too late.

00:50:29.776 --> 00:50:32.654
- What if they need our help?
- It's too dangerous.

00:50:32.863 --> 00:50:34.740
- Why?
- Because if he's killed them...

00:50:34.948 --> 00:50:36.491
...he'll control another EMP.

00:50:38.035 --> 00:50:41.830
At this point, they're on their own.
Just like us.

00:50:43.457 --> 00:50:45.125
Mr. Anderson.

00:50:45.959 --> 00:50:49.963
I see you are as predictable in this world
as you are in the other.

00:50:50.422 --> 00:50:51.965
- What?
- He's out of his mind.

00:50:52.132 --> 00:50:55.093
It might appear that way.
But Mr. Anderson and I know...

00:50:55.260 --> 00:50:58.138
...that appearances can be deceiving.

00:50:58.305 --> 00:51:02.142
Confused, Mr. Anderson?
It'll all become clear in a moment.

00:51:02.309 --> 00:51:05.520
Thank you for bringing me the gun.
You can set it down there.

00:51:05.729 --> 00:51:07.814
Don't do it.

00:51:07.939 --> 00:51:12.152
- Shoot. Shoot now.
- Yes, shoot. Fry us. Burn us alive.

00:51:12.402 --> 00:51:15.655
Do it. If you don't, he'll kill us both.

00:51:16.740 --> 00:51:20.827
Look at him. He knows
he should do it, but he won't.

00:51:20.994 --> 00:51:23.080
- He can't.
- Do it.

00:51:31.588 --> 00:51:35.008
Back away from the gun
and turn around.

00:51:42.015 --> 00:51:43.308
Let her go.

00:51:56.530 --> 00:51:59.533
Somehow familiar, isn't it?

00:51:59.699 --> 00:52:03.870
We've been here before,
you and I, remember?

00:52:04.037 --> 00:52:07.707
I do. I think of nothing else.

00:52:12.295 --> 00:52:15.632
- What do you want?
- I want what you want.

00:52:18.718 --> 00:52:23.098
Yes. That's it, Mr. Anderson.

00:52:23.265 --> 00:52:25.183
Look past the flesh.

00:52:25.392 --> 00:52:30.730
Look through the soft gelatin of these
dull cow eyes and see your enemy.

00:52:32.774 --> 00:52:35.819
- No.
- Oh, yes, Mr. Anderson.

00:52:36.153 --> 00:52:39.114
- It can't be.
- There's nowhere I can't go.

00:52:39.281 --> 00:52:42.158
There is nowhere I won't find you.

00:52:42.325 --> 00:52:46.371
- It's impossible.
- Not impossible.

00:52:46.955 --> 00:52:48.498
Inevitable.

00:52:50.333 --> 00:52:52.335
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

00:52:52.502 --> 00:52:54.171
This is it. It's gotta be.

00:53:39.841 --> 00:53:40.884
Oh, no.

00:53:59.069 --> 00:54:02.948
I wish you could see yourself,
Mr. Anderson.

00:54:07.410 --> 00:54:09.621
Blind messiah.

00:54:13.875 --> 00:54:17.254
You're a symbol for all of your kind,
Mr. Anderson.

00:54:20.090 --> 00:54:22.258
Helpless.

00:54:24.594 --> 00:54:26.763
Pathetic.

00:54:29.683 --> 00:54:33.979
Just waiting to be put out
of your misery.

00:54:39.276 --> 00:54:40.735
I can see you.

00:54:49.619 --> 00:54:52.455
It's not over, Mr. Anderson.

00:54:52.622 --> 00:54:54.499
It's not over.

00:55:07.929 --> 00:55:11.307
- Trinity!
- Neo.

00:55:12.892 --> 00:55:14.310
Neo.

00:55:17.314 --> 00:55:20.483
Oh, no. Your eyes.

00:55:20.650 --> 00:55:22.819
I'll be okay.

00:55:24.154 --> 00:55:26.323
It's all right, Trin.

00:55:28.074 --> 00:55:30.994
But I think you're gonna have to drive.

00:55:37.584 --> 00:55:40.670
Seismic's projecting
22 minutes to breach.

00:55:40.837 --> 00:55:44.507
They can't know we don't have an EMP.
They'll have to attack in waves.

00:55:44.674 --> 00:55:49.345
Concentrate our offense on the diggers.
Order the APUs into position.

00:55:49.596 --> 00:55:51.056
Yes, sir.

00:56:20.877 --> 00:56:23.588
Come on, move.

00:56:55.745 --> 00:56:57.413
All right!

00:56:57.580 --> 00:56:59.415
This is it.

00:56:59.582 --> 00:57:04.629
Now, you all know me,
so I'll just say this as simple as I can.

00:57:05.421 --> 00:57:09.259
If it's our time to die, it's our time.

00:57:09.426 --> 00:57:14.931
All I ask is, if we have
to give these bastards our lives...

00:57:15.098 --> 00:57:17.934
...we give them hell before we do!

00:57:18.184 --> 00:57:20.103
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

00:57:34.909 --> 00:57:37.745
- You scared, Charra?
- Shit, yeah.

00:57:38.788 --> 00:57:40.331
But I'll make you a deal.

00:57:41.040 --> 00:57:44.085
You keep loading, I keep shooting.

00:57:46.296 --> 00:57:48.173
Deal.

00:57:57.640 --> 00:58:00.643
- Holy Christ, would you look at that.
- Quiet.

00:58:01.102 --> 00:58:03.980
- How far to the opening?
- 1.4 kilometers.

00:58:04.230 --> 00:58:08.860
- We're still generating too hot a field.
- Ghost, kill all auxiliary systems.

00:58:09.068 --> 00:58:12.822
- Full manual. Drop down four pads.
- It'll bottom out.

00:58:22.832 --> 00:58:26.169
- Easy, baby.
- Seven hundred meters.

00:58:28.671 --> 00:58:31.341
If we can just get close enough...

00:58:35.845 --> 00:58:37.222
Six hundred meters.

00:58:38.348 --> 00:58:39.974
There.

00:58:47.524 --> 00:58:49.192
Shit!

00:58:51.486 --> 00:58:53.905
- Jig's up, here they come.
- Give me full power.

00:58:54.113 --> 00:58:56.407
Man the gun turrets,
every goddamn one of them. Go!

00:59:13.841 --> 00:59:16.302
I'm coming, baby.

00:59:25.186 --> 00:59:27.188
Here they come.

00:59:31.484 --> 00:59:35.571
<i>- Slow down, this ain't the</i> Logos.
- Hang on to your lunch, here we go.

00:59:44.289 --> 00:59:47.375
Holy Christ, I didn't know
this ship could do that.

01:00:39.260 --> 01:00:40.762
Breach! The dock is breached!

01:01:01.783 --> 01:01:03.743
Knuckle up!

01:01:17.048 --> 01:01:18.674
For Zion!

01:03:26.844 --> 01:03:28.596
Shit.

01:03:33.392 --> 01:03:35.561
Come on, let's go.

01:03:41.275 --> 01:03:42.652
Knuckle up!

01:03:57.792 --> 01:03:59.126
Reload!

01:04:00.878 --> 01:04:02.797
Reload nine!

01:04:09.470 --> 01:04:10.763
Go, go! Move, move!

01:04:23.150 --> 01:04:24.819
Watch your left!

01:04:25.903 --> 01:04:28.155
Don't let them through!

01:04:31.158 --> 01:04:32.660
Zuka!

01:05:09.655 --> 01:05:11.407
Oh, my God.

01:05:24.962 --> 01:05:28.591
Where the hell's my infantry? I want
that goddamn machine taken down!

01:06:02.583 --> 01:06:03.918
Dig this!

01:06:08.089 --> 01:06:09.382
Oh, shit!

01:06:29.110 --> 01:06:30.986
- Yeah!
- Bogey two at the breach point!

01:06:31.195 --> 01:06:32.446
Goddamn it!

01:06:58.472 --> 01:07:00.641
Shit, she's got a fat ass.

01:07:09.942 --> 01:07:13.362
- Keep them off me!
- Christ, there's a shitstorm of them.

01:07:45.269 --> 01:07:47.897
- Captain, you see that?
- They're after the radio. Stop them!

01:07:55.696 --> 01:07:57.031
Damn it!

01:08:21.889 --> 01:08:23.349
Yeah.

01:08:35.069 --> 01:08:36.904
Grab my belt.

01:08:47.373 --> 01:08:48.791
Just give me one clean shot.

01:08:55.673 --> 01:08:57.383
Damn it!

01:09:19.572 --> 01:09:21.157
Charra!

01:09:26.120 --> 01:09:28.789
- I got incoming!
- We got a dock full of incoming!

01:09:28.956 --> 01:09:31.458
- Yes, sir. But this is different, sir.
- What?

01:09:32.126 --> 01:09:33.794
I think it's one of ours, sir.

01:09:33.961 --> 01:09:36.922
- That's impossible.
- Holographics are trying to confirm.

01:09:37.131 --> 01:09:38.841
Contact them.
I want access codes.

01:09:39.049 --> 01:09:41.594
We're trying, sir.
There's no response.

01:09:42.928 --> 01:09:45.639
It's a trick. That's not one of ours,
it can't be.

01:09:45.806 --> 01:09:49.602
That's a mechanical line.
No one can pilot mechanical.

01:09:59.904 --> 01:10:03.157
- Forward aft, 30 degrees at 80 percent.
- Thirty degrees, 80.

01:10:06.160 --> 01:10:09.205
- Lower starboard 60 degrees, 20 percent.
- Sixty degrees.

01:10:12.082 --> 01:10:15.044
- Shit! Come on, keep up!
- I'm trying!

01:10:35.022 --> 01:10:37.733
Sir, holographic confirms.
It's the <i>Hammer</i>, sir.

01:10:38.275 --> 01:10:39.568
How can that be?

01:10:39.777 --> 01:10:41.737
It's under attack, sustaining damage.

01:10:41.946 --> 01:10:44.698
At present velocity,
it'll reach Gate Three in 12 minutes.

01:10:44.865 --> 01:10:47.242
Their EMP could take out every sentinel.

01:10:48.118 --> 01:10:51.538
It'd take out more than that.
It'll wipe out our defense system.

01:10:51.705 --> 01:10:53.916
We blow an EMP inside,
we lose the dock.

01:10:54.541 --> 01:10:56.377
Sir, we already lost the dock.

01:11:00.547 --> 01:11:01.882
Open the gate.

01:11:03.717 --> 01:11:07.930
Gate Three is not responding!
We've taken critical damage, sir!

01:11:08.138 --> 01:11:10.391
We've lost control!
We can't open it!

01:11:20.150 --> 01:11:21.443
There's the exit.

01:11:21.652 --> 01:11:25.072
On my mark, give me full power
90 degrees to lower-left starboard.

01:11:25.572 --> 01:11:27.366
Full power...

01:11:27.574 --> 01:11:28.909
...ninety degrees.

01:11:35.249 --> 01:11:36.542
Now!

01:11:44.049 --> 01:11:46.093
Hold on, baby.

01:11:50.723 --> 01:11:52.599
Goddamn, woman, you can drive.

01:11:52.766 --> 01:11:54.768
We ain't home yet.
What about the gate?

01:11:57.396 --> 01:11:58.856
Sentinels are inside the dock.

01:12:00.232 --> 01:12:01.567
Are we too late?

01:12:31.138 --> 01:12:33.849
- How many APUs are operational?
- Thirteen, sir.

01:12:34.058 --> 01:12:36.018
Get me the one closest to Gate Three.

01:13:04.421 --> 01:13:05.672
Reload!

01:13:05.923 --> 01:13:07.174
He's pissing metal.

01:13:10.677 --> 01:13:12.179
Go!

01:13:26.693 --> 01:13:28.028
Go!

01:13:49.967 --> 01:13:51.718
Heads up! They're coming around!

01:14:04.731 --> 01:14:06.275
Behind you!

01:14:19.830 --> 01:14:21.665
It's jammed!

01:14:27.421 --> 01:14:30.132
Forget it, kid! Get out of here!

01:14:31.258 --> 01:14:32.926
Got it!

01:15:01.413 --> 01:15:03.290
Captain Mifune.

01:15:06.418 --> 01:15:08.295
Oh, no.

01:15:08.795 --> 01:15:10.130
They're coming.

01:15:12.466 --> 01:15:14.092
They're coming.

01:15:15.385 --> 01:15:16.678
The <i>Hammer.</i>

01:15:17.262 --> 01:15:18.639
What?

01:15:19.056 --> 01:15:21.808
You have to open that gate.

01:15:22.601 --> 01:15:24.311
Cut the counterweights.

01:15:26.480 --> 01:15:27.773
You can do it.

01:15:28.649 --> 01:15:31.235
Hurry. There's no time.

01:15:53.674 --> 01:15:55.842
- Lock that down!
- Kill the feeder!

01:15:56.260 --> 01:15:59.346
We won't make it.
We gotta blow the EMP now.

01:15:59.513 --> 01:16:02.683
Come on, someone, please.

01:16:17.364 --> 01:16:19.241
Keep the weight forward.

01:16:21.285 --> 01:16:23.036
Light as a feather.
Light as a feather.

01:16:27.374 --> 01:16:31.378
Holographic reports Captain Mifune's
APU is up and moving to Gate Three.

01:16:37.384 --> 01:16:39.511
Don't over-squeeze the trigger.

01:16:50.188 --> 01:16:52.232
Mifune's APU just reached Gate Three.

01:16:52.399 --> 01:16:55.193
- How much time?
- Two minutes to impact.

01:16:55.902 --> 01:16:59.698
- Captain Mifune, do you copy?
- I think his radio is down, sir.

01:16:59.865 --> 01:17:01.283
Mifune...

01:17:01.491 --> 01:17:03.076
...this is Lock.

01:17:03.327 --> 01:17:06.204
I don't know if you can hear me,
but if you can...

01:17:06.371 --> 01:17:08.707
<i>...the</i> Hammer<i>'s two minutes away.</i>

01:17:09.249 --> 01:17:13.420
<i>You've got two minutes, captain,
to get that gate open.</i>

01:17:15.088 --> 01:17:16.465
Link.

01:17:17.007 --> 01:17:19.259
Get to the main deck!
Charge the EMP!

01:17:55.879 --> 01:17:57.506
Do it, kid.

01:18:01.551 --> 01:18:04.429
Neo. I believe.

01:18:13.480 --> 01:18:15.524
- Yes!
- Can we make it?

01:18:16.900 --> 01:18:18.985
We ain't come this far.

01:18:31.164 --> 01:18:33.375
Almost home, almost home.

01:18:52.853 --> 01:18:54.396
Burn it, Link!

01:19:18.545 --> 01:19:21.548
- You did it.
- No.

01:19:21.882 --> 01:19:23.508
We did it.

01:19:24.551 --> 01:19:25.927
You're a hell of a pilot.

01:19:39.649 --> 01:19:40.984
Link!

01:19:41.651 --> 01:19:43.320
- Zee? Zee!
- Link!

01:19:50.327 --> 01:19:53.121
I knew you'd come. I knew it.

01:19:53.830 --> 01:19:55.790
I made a promise.

01:20:13.892 --> 01:20:15.894
Three captains, one ship.

01:20:16.061 --> 01:20:20.065
I'll assume the other ships were lost
under equally pointless circumstances.

01:20:20.232 --> 01:20:21.858
Good to see you too, Jason.

01:20:22.067 --> 01:20:24.402
The Council's waiting to hear
your explanation.

01:20:24.569 --> 01:20:28.698
Forgive me for not attending,
but I have to try to salvage this debacle.

01:20:29.491 --> 01:20:32.077
Did I miss something?
I thought we saved the dock.

01:20:32.244 --> 01:20:34.079
That's the problem with you people.

01:20:34.246 --> 01:20:36.790
You can't think but five minutes
in front of you.

01:20:37.082 --> 01:20:40.710
That EMP knocked out almost every
piece of hardware and every APU.

01:20:40.877 --> 01:20:43.797
If I were the machines,
I'd send every sentinel here now.

01:20:44.089 --> 01:20:47.759
Save the dock, captain?
You handed it to them on a silver platter.

01:20:53.515 --> 01:20:55.475
Come on, get it cut.

01:20:57.102 --> 01:20:58.436
The bridge is clear.

01:21:01.022 --> 01:21:02.899
Do you hear that?

01:21:05.277 --> 01:21:06.778
Get that cable run!

01:21:07.028 --> 01:21:10.782
- I want the system back online!
- It's the dock. They've got incoming.

01:21:12.117 --> 01:21:14.452
Order everyone to fall back.

01:21:14.619 --> 01:21:17.330
Seal the shaft. Now.

01:21:18.123 --> 01:21:19.749
Move it!

01:21:23.128 --> 01:21:24.796
Oh, my God.

01:21:32.929 --> 01:21:35.140
- All clear.
- Do it.

01:21:35.307 --> 01:21:37.475
- Go! Come on! Run!
- Go!

01:21:53.783 --> 01:21:55.327
Your move.

01:21:56.494 --> 01:21:58.163
So you gave them your ship?

01:21:58.663 --> 01:22:02.834
- That is correct, councillor, I did.
- Knowing what he planned to do with it?

01:22:04.502 --> 01:22:06.338
The Oracle said nothing of this?

01:22:07.339 --> 01:22:11.843
She told me Neo would need my help,
and I would choose to help him or not.

01:22:12.177 --> 01:22:16.640
But what hope can a single vessel have
against their entire defense system?

01:22:16.848 --> 01:22:20.018
None. It's completely impossible.
But he wouldn't listen.

01:22:20.185 --> 01:22:24.522
He wouldn't even take any ammunition.
He was totally out of his goddamn mind.

01:22:24.689 --> 01:22:27.525
No, he wasn't.

01:22:29.319 --> 01:22:31.988
Neo is doing what he believes
he must do.

01:22:33.365 --> 01:22:36.618
I don't know if what he's doing is right.
I don't know...

01:22:36.826 --> 01:22:39.412
...if he'll reach the machine city.

01:22:39.621 --> 01:22:42.874
And if he does, I don't know
what he can do to save us.

01:22:44.209 --> 01:22:48.880
But I do know that as long as there is
a single breath in his body...

01:22:50.340 --> 01:22:52.384
...he will not give up.

01:22:53.718 --> 01:22:55.220
And neither can we.

01:23:01.685 --> 01:23:03.019
Temperature's dropping.

01:23:06.564 --> 01:23:07.899
Here we go.

01:23:47.439 --> 01:23:49.149
We're over the fields, aren't we?

01:23:50.608 --> 01:23:51.943
How do you know that?

01:23:52.694 --> 01:23:54.529
I can feel them.

01:24:03.288 --> 01:24:04.956
Over there.

01:24:05.749 --> 01:24:09.627
There's our path. Can you see it?
Three lines.

01:24:09.794 --> 01:24:11.129
Power lines.

01:24:12.088 --> 01:24:13.840
Follow them.

01:24:30.815 --> 01:24:32.650
What are they doing?

01:24:32.817 --> 01:24:34.527
I don't know.

01:24:35.487 --> 01:24:37.322
Lieutenant?

01:24:52.504 --> 01:24:53.838
Goddamn it.

01:24:54.172 --> 01:24:55.507
What do we do now?

01:25:00.178 --> 01:25:02.263
It is now a matter of time.

01:25:03.014 --> 01:25:05.517
The machines will breach
the walls of this city.

01:25:06.851 --> 01:25:11.356
I recommend that the Council join the
non-military personnel inside the temple.

01:25:12.023 --> 01:25:13.358
How long do we have?

01:25:13.858 --> 01:25:16.528
Two hours. Maybe less.

01:25:18.321 --> 01:25:22.534
My men have fortified the entrance with
enough artillery to make our last stand.

01:25:24.369 --> 01:25:26.871
Beyond that, there isn't anything more
I can do.

01:25:27.372 --> 01:25:30.875
Commander, do you think that
we have any chance of surviving?

01:25:32.544 --> 01:25:35.046
If I were you, I wouldn't
ask me that question.

01:25:36.214 --> 01:25:37.549
I would ask him.

01:25:38.383 --> 01:25:42.053
- Why?
- He's the one who believes in miracles.

01:25:49.352 --> 01:25:51.896
There. Those mountains.

01:25:52.814 --> 01:25:54.607
That's it.

01:25:57.986 --> 01:25:59.904
- Do you see what's out there?
- Yes.

01:26:00.405 --> 01:26:03.074
If you tell me we'll make it,
I'll believe you.

01:26:03.199 --> 01:26:04.909
We'll make it.

01:26:07.912 --> 01:26:09.581
We have to.

01:27:22.904 --> 01:27:24.614
Sentinels.

01:27:35.959 --> 01:27:36.417
There's too many!

01:27:54.018 --> 01:27:55.353
Gotcha!

01:27:56.020 --> 01:27:58.189
- I need help here!
- I can't beat them.

01:27:58.439 --> 01:28:00.858
- What do we do?
- Go up, over them.

01:28:01.109 --> 01:28:04.070
- What?
- The sky! It's the only way.

01:28:06.030 --> 01:28:07.782
Then up we go.

01:28:43.067 --> 01:28:44.902
Beautiful.

01:29:06.758 --> 01:29:09.427
Pump the igniter. The ship will start.

01:29:16.851 --> 01:29:19.270
Again. Slowly.

01:29:22.273 --> 01:29:23.775
Now!

01:29:49.258 --> 01:29:50.760
Trin?

01:29:52.804 --> 01:29:54.639
Trinity?

01:29:55.723 --> 01:29:57.350
Trinity?

01:29:58.559 --> 01:30:00.645
- I'm here.
- Where?

01:30:00.770 --> 01:30:02.146
Here.

01:30:12.448 --> 01:30:13.825
We made it.

01:30:15.576 --> 01:30:17.370
You said we would.

01:30:19.664 --> 01:30:22.166
It's unbelievable, Trin.

01:30:23.167 --> 01:30:24.836
Light everywhere.

01:30:25.169 --> 01:30:28.005
Like the whole thing was built of light.

01:30:28.673 --> 01:30:30.800
I wish you could see what I see.

01:30:32.468 --> 01:30:34.512
You've already shown me so much.

01:30:36.764 --> 01:30:40.059
What is it, Trinity?
What's wrong?

01:30:41.477 --> 01:30:43.938
I can't go with you, Neo.

01:30:45.648 --> 01:30:47.400
I've gone as far as I can.

01:30:47.692 --> 01:30:49.068
What?

01:30:52.029 --> 01:30:53.489
Oh, no.

01:30:54.365 --> 01:30:56.075
Oh, no. No, no.

01:30:56.868 --> 01:30:58.536
It's all right.

01:30:59.871 --> 01:31:01.539
It's time.

01:31:03.124 --> 01:31:05.585
I've done all that I could do.

01:31:06.836 --> 01:31:09.213
Now you have to do the rest.

01:31:09.964 --> 01:31:12.049
You have to finish it.

01:31:12.383 --> 01:31:14.552
You have to save Zion.

01:31:15.052 --> 01:31:16.679
I can't.

01:31:17.180 --> 01:31:20.516
- Not without you.
- Yes, you can.

01:31:21.058 --> 01:31:22.727
You will.

01:31:23.728 --> 01:31:26.898
I believe it. I always have.

01:31:29.358 --> 01:31:30.985
Trinity.

01:31:33.237 --> 01:31:36.699
Trinity, you can't die.

01:31:38.743 --> 01:31:40.870
You can't.

01:31:41.162 --> 01:31:42.747
You can't.

01:31:42.914 --> 01:31:45.082
Yes, I can.

01:31:48.252 --> 01:31:50.630
You brought me back once.

01:31:52.882 --> 01:31:54.926
But not this time.

01:32:00.848 --> 01:32:02.767
Do you remember...

01:32:04.560 --> 01:32:07.438
...on that roof, after you caught me...

01:32:09.065 --> 01:32:10.816
...the last thing I said to you?

01:32:13.569 --> 01:32:15.112
You said, "I'm sorry."

01:32:16.447 --> 01:32:18.532
I wish I hadn't.

01:32:21.619 --> 01:32:23.913
That was my last thought.

01:32:26.290 --> 01:32:29.126
I wished I had one more chance...

01:32:30.044 --> 01:32:32.296
...to say what really mattered.

01:32:34.882 --> 01:32:37.677
To say how much I loved you.

01:32:40.096 --> 01:32:43.474
How grateful I was for every moment
I was with you.

01:32:46.269 --> 01:32:51.190
But by the time I knew how to say
what I wanted to, it was too late.

01:32:57.280 --> 01:32:59.824
But you brought me back.

01:33:02.743 --> 01:33:04.120
You gave me my wish.

01:33:08.291 --> 01:33:12.336
One more chance to say
what I really wanted to say.

01:33:17.008 --> 01:33:18.843
Kiss me.

01:33:21.846 --> 01:33:23.639
Once more...

01:33:25.349 --> 01:33:26.726
...kiss me.

01:33:54.128 --> 01:33:56.213
Get that ammunition where it belongs!

01:33:56.339 --> 01:33:58.215
You got one chance to get this right.

01:33:58.883 --> 01:34:00.718
Get that damn thing mounted!

01:34:05.723 --> 01:34:08.267
- Hurry.
- Let's go, let's go, let's go!

01:34:23.157 --> 01:34:24.492
Neo...

01:34:24.825 --> 01:34:27.244
...if you're gonna do something,
do it quick.

01:36:36.040 --> 01:36:38.083
I only ask to say
what I've come to say.

01:36:38.292 --> 01:36:42.087
After that, do what you want,
and I won't try and stop you.

01:36:46.217 --> 01:36:47.551
Speak.

01:36:48.344 --> 01:36:51.263
The program Smith has grown
beyond your control.

01:36:51.472 --> 01:36:54.892
Soon he will spread through this city
as he spread through the Matrix.

01:36:55.059 --> 01:36:56.393
You cannot stop him.

01:36:58.479 --> 01:37:00.773
- But I can.
- We don't need you!

01:37:01.816 --> 01:37:04.109
We need nothing!

01:37:05.236 --> 01:37:09.114
If that's true, then I've made a mistake,
and you should kill me now.

01:37:14.245 --> 01:37:16.080
What do you want?

01:37:17.498 --> 01:37:18.749
Peace.

01:37:44.608 --> 01:37:46.485
What are they doing?

01:37:52.116 --> 01:37:54.118
What are you doing?

01:37:57.288 --> 01:37:59.164
Morpheus!

01:38:23.564 --> 01:38:25.524
And if you fail?

01:38:27.818 --> 01:38:29.778
I won't.

01:38:51.258 --> 01:38:52.843
Neo.

01:38:52.968 --> 01:38:54.595
He fights for us.

01:39:36.387 --> 01:39:39.264
Mr. Anderson, welcome back.

01:39:39.473 --> 01:39:41.600
We missed you.

01:39:45.729 --> 01:39:48.607
You like what I've done with the place?

01:39:49.233 --> 01:39:50.901
It ends tonight.

01:39:51.902 --> 01:39:54.905
I know it does. I've seen it.

01:39:55.072 --> 01:39:58.784
That's why the rest of me
is just going to enjoy the show...

01:39:58.992 --> 01:40:02.621
...because we already know
that I'm the one that beats you.

01:41:54.942 --> 01:41:57.820
Can you feel it, Mr. Anderson...

01:41:58.028 --> 01:42:00.405
...closing in on you?

01:42:00.614 --> 01:42:02.741
Oh, I can.

01:42:04.117 --> 01:42:08.205
I really should thank you for it.
After all, it was your life...

01:42:08.372 --> 01:42:12.042
...that taught me the purpose of all life.

01:42:12.459 --> 01:42:15.921
The purpose of life is to end.

01:45:51.845 --> 01:45:53.764
Why, Mr. Anderson?

01:45:53.889 --> 01:45:57.768
Why, why, why?

01:45:57.934 --> 01:45:59.269
Why do you do it?

01:46:00.020 --> 01:46:01.980
Why? Why get up?

01:46:02.189 --> 01:46:03.982
Why keep fighting?

01:46:05.525 --> 01:46:07.986
Do you believe you're fighting
for something?

01:46:08.195 --> 01:46:10.822
For more than your survival?

01:46:11.031 --> 01:46:14.284
Can you tell me what it is?
Do you even know?

01:46:17.788 --> 01:46:19.498
Is it freedom or truth?

01:46:19.706 --> 01:46:22.042
Perhaps peace? Could it be for love?

01:46:22.250 --> 01:46:25.629
Illusions, Mr. Anderson.
Vagaries of perception.

01:46:26.046 --> 01:46:29.132
Temporary constructs
of a feeble human intellect...

01:46:29.299 --> 01:46:31.885
...trying desperately
to justify an existence...

01:46:32.094 --> 01:46:34.137
...that is without meaning or purpose!

01:46:34.304 --> 01:46:37.766
And all of them as artificial
as the Matrix itself...

01:46:37.933 --> 01:46:44.022
...although only a human mind could
invent something as insipid as love.

01:46:46.566 --> 01:46:48.652
You must be able to see it,
Mr. Anderson.

01:46:48.819 --> 01:46:53.365
You must know it by now. You can't
win. It's pointless to keep fighting.

01:46:56.159 --> 01:46:59.371
Why, Mr. Anderson, why?
Why do you persist?

01:47:02.666 --> 01:47:04.876
Because I choose to.

01:48:09.858 --> 01:48:12.903
This is my world! My world!

01:48:37.594 --> 01:48:39.304
Wait.

01:48:39.513 --> 01:48:41.640
I've seen this.

01:48:42.849 --> 01:48:45.143
This is it. This is the end.

01:48:46.853 --> 01:48:50.774
Yes. You were laying right there,
just like that.

01:48:50.899 --> 01:48:53.276
And I... I...

01:48:53.443 --> 01:48:59.282
I stand here, right here,
and I'm supposed to say something.

01:49:01.284 --> 01:49:04.788
"Everything that has a beginning
has an end, Neo."

01:49:13.547 --> 01:49:17.259
What? What did I just say?

01:49:22.639 --> 01:49:26.476
No, no. This isn't right.
This can't be right.

01:49:33.984 --> 01:49:35.652
Get away from me!

01:49:35.819 --> 01:49:37.195
What are you afraid of?

01:49:37.988 --> 01:49:39.322
It's a trick.

01:49:39.990 --> 01:49:42.200
You were right, Smith.

01:49:43.159 --> 01:49:44.995
You were always right.

01:49:48.290 --> 01:49:50.000
It was inevitable.

01:50:21.781 --> 01:50:23.366
Is it over?

01:50:54.397 --> 01:50:56.733
Oh, no, no, no.

01:50:56.900 --> 01:50:58.443
No, it's not fair.

01:51:52.789 --> 01:51:55.125
It is done.

01:52:27.073 --> 01:52:29.367
It doesn't make sense.

01:52:33.329 --> 01:52:34.080
He did it.

01:52:35.749 --> 01:52:37.959
He saved us.

01:52:38.251 --> 01:52:40.378
He saved us.

01:52:41.004 --> 01:52:44.215
It's over! He did it! He did it!

01:52:44.507 --> 01:52:45.842
He did it! It's over!

01:52:46.009 --> 01:52:48.470
It's over! He did it! He did it!

01:52:48.678 --> 01:52:50.263
- What is it? What happened?

01:52:50.263 --> 01:52:51.222
- Sir, he ended the war.

01:52:51.431 --> 01:52:53.308
The machines, they're gone.

01:52:53.516 --> 01:52:56.811
The war is over, sir. The war is over.

01:52:58.438 --> 01:53:01.816
Zion! Zion!

01:53:02.025 --> 01:53:03.776
Zion, it's over!

01:53:04.110 --> 01:53:05.612
It's over!

01:53:05.779 --> 01:53:08.448
The war is over!

01:53:08.573 --> 01:53:11.451
The war is over!

01:53:11.618 --> 01:53:14.120
Whoo!

01:53:32.764 --> 01:53:35.683
I have imagined this moment...

01:53:36.226 --> 01:53:38.478
...for so long.

01:53:42.398 --> 01:53:44.150
Is this real?

01:53:52.992 --> 01:53:55.829
Neo, wherever you are...

01:53:56.830 --> 01:53:58.873
...thank you.

01:54:42.709 --> 01:54:44.043
Good morning.

01:55:05.315 --> 01:55:09.193
Well, now. Ain't this a surprise.

01:55:09.652 --> 01:55:11.779
You played a very dangerous game.

01:55:11.988 --> 01:55:14.240
Change always is.

01:55:14.824 --> 01:55:18.119
Just how long do you think
this peace is going to last?

01:55:19.495 --> 01:55:20.830
As long as it can.

01:55:25.001 --> 01:55:26.961
What about the others?

01:55:28.671 --> 01:55:30.089
What others?

01:55:30.256 --> 01:55:31.883
The ones that want out.

01:55:32.675 --> 01:55:34.761
Obviously, they will be freed.

01:55:35.345 --> 01:55:36.971
I have your word?

01:55:37.180 --> 01:55:40.933
What do you think I am? Human?

01:55:54.947 --> 01:55:56.491
Oracle!

01:56:03.373 --> 01:56:05.500
We were afraid we might not find you.

01:56:05.708 --> 01:56:08.336
Everything's okay now.

01:56:08.878 --> 01:56:10.630
Look, look.

01:56:11.214 --> 01:56:13.633
Just look at that.

01:56:14.300 --> 01:56:16.969
Beautiful.

01:56:17.887 --> 01:56:20.306
Did you do that?

01:56:20.640 --> 01:56:22.809
For Neo.

01:56:23.142 --> 01:56:25.103
That's nice.

01:56:25.311 --> 01:56:26.980
I know he'd love it.

01:56:27.647 --> 01:56:29.649
Will we ever see him again?

01:56:30.233 --> 01:56:32.944
I suspect so.

01:56:33.152 --> 01:56:34.821
Someday.

01:56:39.659 --> 01:56:41.452
Did you always know?

01:56:41.619 --> 01:56:44.872
Oh, no. No, I didn't.

01:56:45.415 --> 01:56:48.000
But I believed.

01:56:48.918 --> 01:56:51.337
I believed.
